  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Fri Apr 17 2026\n\nMuch Cooler and Dry Conditions: Northwest flow aloft will allow\nfor much cooler and drier conditions to filter into the area for\nthe rest of the weekend. Surface high pressure looks to slide\nclose to the area Saturday night into Sunday morning. If skies\ncan clear and winds remain light, we could see some frost\npotential. Latest NBM shows a corridor of 40-60% probs of temps\ndropping below 36 degrees across the heart of the Ozark Plateau\nand eastern Ozarks. Those with agricultural interests will want\nto stay up on the forecast. A gradual warm up is expected next \nweek with no significant systems through mid week.",
